          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first partnership to collect exactly 10 game points. Going over 10 reduces score to 7; losing all tricks reduces score to 0.',
          gameplay: "Player to dealer's left leads to first trick. Must follow suit if able. If no trumps yet, may play any card when void. Once trumps exist, must play trump if void in led suit. Must beat highest card played if able (even partner's card).",
          keyRules: [
            "Follow suit if able; if void in led suit and trumps exist must play trump; must beat highest card in trick if able (even partner's).",
            'Only trick winner may attempt one marriage declaration before leading to next trick; first declaration sets trumps for the hand.',
            'Win by reaching exactly 10 game points; over 10 reduces to 7; no tricks in a hand reduces score to 0.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Try to win early tricks so you can declare trumps if you have a marriage. The first marriage declaration is crucial as it sets trumps for the whole hand.',
          intermediate: "Decide whether to declare your own marriage or ask partner. Declaring yourself gives 2 points and sets trumps immediately. Asking partner can be safer but 'breaks' your own marriages. Track which marriages have been 'broken'.",
          advanced: "The 'half marriage' declaration can be a clever tactic - it breaks all marriages in both hands, preventing opponents from declaring trumps later. Timing when to declare is key: too early and opponents know the trump suit; too late and opponent might declare first.",
          tips: [
            'If you have multiple marriages, you might declare a non-trump one first (if you can win another trick) for the extra game point',
            'The last trick is worth 1 game point - fight for it, especially in close games',
            "If you're at 9 game points, focus on getting exactly 1 more - avoid the 'over 10' penalty",
            "Remember: you must beat your partner's card if you can, even if you'd rather let them win!",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
